{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:50:08.049741Z","id":"26fd1d7e6cc6b66aede9e2accd39cd17c1086be0ca86d6279e920fc7599b9b28","body":{"detail":"versionFiles reads GET /api/remotes/{rid}/artifacts/{raid}/versions/{n}/files as {version: {files: {path: meta}}} (the shape of a version's GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions/{n}), then fetches each file at .../files/{path}; apps accepts GET /api/remotes/{rid}/apps as a bare list (GET /api/hosted/apps) or {apps: [...]}. Both routes are added by the core's app mode in crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs; test/remote/remote_api_test.dart drives them through a fake ClaxTransport answering these shapes. Check them against the routes once they land, and drop whichever apps shape the core does not serve.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":306},"end":{"line":340},"content_hash":"c08ffab193fb21d6c15617536d91b13e1cf4cbb7cd38308dec5c1a604f016a7f"},"summary":"versionFiles and apps parse answer shapes the core's routes do not serve yet","tags":["remote","contract","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:50:08.049818Z","id":"30c417880f5e034bf782dc09212ff7bc6255fb172619067c64771f0d38b2871d","body":{"detail":"Deleting the recipient's web-head guard (b.version > link.baseRemoteVersion), the recipient's held-bundle guard (b.bundleVersion > held), or the author's unmoved-head content check (head.version == base && head.contentSha256 != liveContentSha256) is caught by a row in test/remote/sync_state_test.dart's table, but not by its property test: in the histories its model (_World) generates, the base and the held bundle version move together and the unmoved head's content is always the last release, so each guard is redundant with another there. A state where they differ (a recipient linked at a base without taking that base's bundle, or a live version that is not the head it claims) can only come from a caller that writes AppLink fields inconsistently.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"6f6dad83184c465622be132d2138a343776f5ed9fb1271a223db5a1cd8bff085"},"summary":"Three syncState guards are pinned only by table rows: the random-history property test never reaches them","tags":["remote","tests","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/fake_remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:50:08.049936Z","id":"64b5b85ea39980c6202417cbef00e6b4078f7789790678a23f23ad0f3f95a983","body":{"detail":"FakeRemoteApi.putBundle refuses different bytes on a version that carries a bundle (400 bundle_exists) and a bundle version that does not go up (400 bundle_version). The hosted PUT /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions/{n}/bundle route answers 400 with the store's own codes, which crates/clax-store did not define when the fake was written. Match them once the route lands, so tests against the fake see the codes the core passes through.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":440},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"3b96fe9e1132a8fdbbe7c1dd58d2df62362d8a46e6630c2b9177190c089a0a49"},"summary":"FakeRemoteApi's bundle refusal codes bundle_exists and bundle_version are placeholders for the store's","tags":["remote","fakes","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:55:08.202889Z","id":"b195a8dd37f6169747587b32262e91cd3c75ecccde9b35f9cd9a26ea7b3d5b94","body":{"detail":"_artifact (remote_api.dart:410-425) accepts an http:// artifact address on any host, and anonymousBundle accepts any absolute URL a head's bundle.url names, including http and another origin than the head's. crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:90-105 takes a remote only as https, or http on localhost. With the linked trust row (lib/bundle/trust.dart:112-118) a bundle from the linked public copy is an update whatever key signed it, so for an app got by an http://host/a/ID link anyone on the path can serve a higher version of its lineage and it is offered as that app's update.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":295},"end":{"line":304},"content_hash":"3badb4207f03a7b5e4bdfab6b0d5f988dfafb37592cb9b7721509f710c15abac"},"suggested_fix":"Apply the core's rule in _artifact and anonymousBundle: https, or http only on localhost/loopback; refuse a bundle.url on another origin than the head's. Add remote_api_test vectors.","summary":"The anonymous routes fetch over plain http from any host, unlike the core's https-or-localhost rule for remotes","tags":["review","trust","remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/fake_remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:55:08.203053Z","id":"3b3e241b7700913090f8e57138f7c3d9002f536da0063bcb357eb1737a1054ac","body":{"detail":"putBundle checks only that the app has a link, the version exists and the bundle version goes up. A link made with link() to a copy whose access is viewer or commenter (FakePublicCopy.access) accepts a bundle, where the hosted PUT bundle route refuses a token without the update right (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.8, editors' pushes). It also accepts a lineage other than the copy's earlier bundles' (§5.8: one lineage per public copy). Tests against the fake can then pass a flow the real remote refuses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":412},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"00f82398b8d691a92d91848105ce8910c0d45a26c92da0b6b09ff208121c97b3"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse 403 not_permitted unless access is owner or editor, and refuse a lineage that differs from bundled?.bundle?.lineage with the hosted route's code; add both to fake_remote_api_test.","summary":"FakeRemoteApi.putBundle takes a bundle on a copy the account may not publish, and of any lineage","tags":["review","fakes","remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:55:08.203478Z","id":"a544154c30a87663c12e5fee5dde45abdb5a213027b0d7f7af22a7e77297a56d","body":{"detail":"Future.wait starts one transport.send per path the remote lists, all concurrently, and keeps every body in memory, with no cap on the number of files or their sum (the bundle routes cap at bundleCap, 32 MiB). A web-made head with thousands of files, or a remote answering with a huge list, opens that many requests through the core at once and holds them all; one failure leaves the others running.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":306},"end":{"line":327},"content_hash":"c0c6cefc95a032a04bf2b01905e4c285599df27a4fc4476c53c4325d2599fa85"},"suggested_fix":"Fetch with a small fixed concurrency and stop past maxBundleBytes in total (413 bundle_too_large), or have the core serve the version's files in one response.","summary":"versionFiles fetches every file at once with no count or total size limit","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/fake_remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.784880Z","id":"936685c22307e497f793e3931e416c6d3ac9c11ba4435086bab2093dcf0f5e7e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"64b5b85ea39980c6202417cbef00e6b4078f7789790678a23f23ad0f3f95a983","summary":"The codes added since (bundle_mismatch, bundle_lineage, and not_permitted for a copy the account may not publish) are placeholders too: Publisher (lib/remote/publisher.dart _upload) drops a pending bundle on any non-transient refusal and shows the message, so only the hosted route's status matters to it today.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785096Z","id":"ee8a1ad03aca08809e1a377ec9d2d9939669073592f9c00ac97552176ae858aa","body":{"detail":"Publisher.publish lands an earlier pending bundle first, but two calls that start together both pass that check. The core's publish replays and orders the pushes; the first bundle's upload then finds its pending record replaced (_drop leaves it) and may upload after the second, which the remote refuses as bundle_version. No test drives concurrent publishes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"d18c71be75cfe32f9223523a61f465a8338cb695378ba777fd685d07a6be22f5"},"summary":"Two publishes of the same app at once are not serialized: both export and push, and the second's pending record replaces the first's","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785129Z","id":"a3807ca94897d6148bd473397fd406d4334344df0ae03f3cf7d4e3280b0c245a","body":{"detail":"_upload drops the pending record and its bytes on any non-transient ClaxApiError (403, 400 bundle_*, 413). The public version stays, so pulls of the copy get the previous bundle (the head names the latest version that carries one) until the next publish.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":253},"content_hash":"b0f914c0d84eab45d478aa6c4cd766dc88320d9cbcc97dd8dcf38b82c14d765d"},"summary":"A bundle the remote refuses outright leaves its public version without a bundle, with only the refusal message to show for it","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/fake_remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.969920Z","id":"22c29e1307d3a8119d0427dd68b9842d52f70ab0486b64989d0fc967d26a7eff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e1d881a42","summary":"FakeRemoteApi.putBundle now refuses 403 not_permitted for a copy the account may not publish (access not owner or editor), 400 bundle_mismatch for a content hash other than its version's, and 400 bundle_lineage for a lineage other than the copy's last bundle's; test/remote/fake_remote_api_test.dart covers each, and //apps/clax_app:remote_fake_remote_api_test PASSED under just test-affected at 0cca94805.","supersedes":"3b3e241b7700913090f8e57138f7c3d9002f536da0063bcb357eb1737a1054ac","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/puller.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:06:11.766882Z","id":"3b528a257b3f8988a5e06dedde36b336a9c014b47e601089465a2f2b2eccfe5e","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.13 says pulls never bring documents. Scratch mutation at puller.dart:190 (seed kept): //apps/clax_app:remote_puller_test PASSED under just test-affected; only dart_analyze failed, for the then-unused _withoutSeed. copyOf in puller_test.dart:38-59 makes bundles without a seed, so the rule is never reached.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":283},"content_hash":"7b5b0c6f5d4cb1efa0aae889760fb1495460cc49517a6ee49091f4cf17e429c4"},"suggested_fix":"Add a pull of a bundle made with a seed and assert the installed app has no documents and the install sheet's BundleSummary.seedDocs is null.","summary":"No test pins that a pull brings no documents: replacing installer.openRead(_withoutSeed(bundle), …) at line 190 with openRead(bundle, …) leaves test/remote/puller_test.dart passing","tags":["review","tests","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:06:11.766951Z","id":"6b77c6f1c7a12d68c13153584a87b714669afcb147195e4445df84165431be36","body":{"detail":"Without the block, a publish made while an earlier bundle is still pending exports and pushes first, then its store.update (publisher.dart:170-194) replaces pendingBundle, so the earlier public version never gets its bundle. Scratch mutation: //apps/clax_app:remote_publisher_test PASSED under just test-affected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"098bbf87b472754a0ca856925534fb18a21470619dae143ba8de2f06a37fc48c"},"suggested_fix":"A test that fails putBundle offline, starts a second publish of the same app, and asserts both public versions end with their own bundles in order.","summary":"No test pins that a publish lands an earlier pending bundle first: deleting lines 127-129 leaves test/remote/publisher_test.dart passing","tags":["review","tests","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:06:11.768264Z","id":"3f9115c0210938e0376dd31f974f10c2da620837bec22cf52b19f344f1be8c0b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ee8a1ad03aca08809e1a377ec9d2d9939669073592f9c00ac97552176ae858aa","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"d18c71be75cfe32f9223523a61f465a8338cb695378ba777fd685d07a6be22f5"},"summary":"Concrete failures when two publishes of one app interleave: both write <support>/publishing/<aid>.clax.tmp (publisher.dart:167-169), so one rename can fail after its push succeeded (Refused, version left without bundle) or one upload can read the other's bytes under its own PendingBundle (a bundle on the wrong public version that every recipient then refuses as a hash mismatch, puller.dart:174-181); both exports read the same entry.version, so both bundles carry the same bundle version and the second put is refused; and whichever store.update runs last sets baseRemoteVersion, so it can go back to the earlier public version and the device's next publish is refused as moved against its own version. No UI path reaches it today (the progress sheet is modal), but an automatic publish after each change would.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:06:11.769540Z","id":"20e8bd74d3a60552d463f67006446517753f8623784395efb9f4c441cfb73344","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a3807ca94897d6148bd473397fd406d4334344df0ae03f3cf7d4e3280b0c245a","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":253},"content_hash":"b0f914c0d84eab45d478aa6c4cd766dc88320d9cbcc97dd8dcf38b82c14d765d"},"summary":"What follows from it: the person sees the remote's raw message (e.g. FakeRemoteApi's 'the bundle is not this version's files') as a failure although the version is public; recipients keep being offered the previous version that has a bundle (spec §5.9, like a web-made version); and the author's own device reads its own version as web-made (head.bundle.version != head.version), so lib/remote/sync_state.dart answers updateWaiting or diverged for it until the next publish.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/puller.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:03:23.661982Z","id":"2458f71821b3e192ff16dc13bf315f636668d909945de5e887c067d5469e0d21","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4eb6cb3ab","summary":"test/remote/puller_test.dart 'a pull brings no documents, though the bundle carries some' pulls a bundle with three seed docs and expects none written; it passes (just test-affected a6028f8d2 at be347b362: 'Executed 239 out of 284 tests: 284 tests pass.') and failed with openRead(bundle, …) in place of _withoutSeed(bundle).","supersedes":"3b528a257b3f8988a5e06dedde36b336a9c014b47e601089465a2f2b2eccfe5e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:03:23.848433Z","id":"16278a5a66b53bbb37631fe410e2c5e3c0710b479d3f41feb7f743d8be56912e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e1a8e4dd1","summary":"test/remote/publisher_test.dart 'a publish while an earlier bundle is pending lands that one first, so each public version keeps its own bundle' passes (just test-affected a6028f8d2 at be347b362: 'Executed 239 out of 284 tests: 284 tests pass.') and failed with the pending-first block removed.","supersedes":"6b77c6f1c7a12d68c13153584a87b714669afcb147195e4445df84165431be36","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:03:24.113073Z","id":"cdd6512823207fae6c3963d746aff29b51110d2b53150f97eb960e421628626f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e1a8e4dd1","summary":"Publisher.publish now chains each app's publishes (_publishing), so one runs at a time, and each bundle goes through its own temporary file (<aid>.clax.<pid>_<n>.tmp). test/remote/publisher_test.dart 'two publishes of one app at once run one after the other' passes (just test-affected a6028f8d2 at be347b362: 'Executed 239 out of 284 tests: 284 tests pass.') and failed with the chain removed.","supersedes":"ee8a1ad03aca08809e1a377ec9d2d9939669073592f9c00ac97552176ae858aa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:07:48.307287Z","id":"295ef1c38ec20002c81156f41564edb4b3f7b8497d59f41768d0aed361e47fd3","body":{"detail":"The export (record: false) snapshots the entry before the push, and store.update at publisher.dart:209-230 returns made.copyWith(link: …) whatever the store holds then; only the link is taken from the current entry. The push can wait for a connection for a long time in the background, now that the progress sheet closes (lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:183-188). Failure: an update or a Keep mine that lands on the entry during that wait is reverted to the snapshot's version, released and updatesStopped; an app deleted during the wait (its entry dropped) gets its entry written again, since e == null no longer returns null.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":205},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"7b103fea6a8a61104d1319ab54b250e2dc1e3945bdabfc98ca84eda557cb5a68"},"suggested_fix":"Apply the release to the current entry (withRelease on e) and skip the write when e is null unless this is the app's first export; or refuse the write when e.version moved since the export.","summary":"After the push, Publisher writes the export-time lineage entry whole: whatever changed in the entry meanwhile is undone, and a deleted app's entry comes back","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:07:48.307392Z","id":"e28fa960c66102079834f2bd7a0f647111c3e31fee02327cbeddb0dd655b7676","body":{"detail":"Publisher passes the copy's latest bundle version from its head as Exporter.export's atLeast, so a linked publish's bundle version goes past both the entry's and the copy's (spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.8). A test is feasible with FakeRemoteApi: publish v1, set the copy's last version's FakeBundle to bundleVersion 9 (FakeBundle is assignable, as test/remote/puller_test.dart:52 does), publish v2, and expect Published with bundle version 10; without the floor the fake refuses the bundle (version does not go up). The state it guards (base at the head, entry.version behind the copy's last bundle) is not reached by Task 9's flows alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"3b29f066e36936aec2c5fa4b38081dfb34d5fae03008f8bd481089a381713b1b"},"suggested_fix":"Add the test described before the flows that can leave the entry behind (merge, take theirs) land.","summary":"No test pins the head floor (atLeast): removing it leaves test/remote/publisher_test.dart passing","tags":["review","tests","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/fake_remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:25:25.909257Z","id":"2421136325f581e612f2cdbd570ac91cf2f839a89004ace68ce69cc70ac704dc","body":{"detail":"clax-store's add_pending_remote (crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:203-218) deletes a pending remote at the same origin before inserting the new one, so the core holds at most one pending sign-in per origin; the fake adds a second. The remote refuses a client name over 64 characters or with a control character (crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:462), surfaced by the core as 502 remote_refused; the fake accepts any `machine`. A test of Try again or of a long device name passes against the fake where the core answers differently.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":299},"end":{"line":330},"content_hash":"179ba230fefab89b9238215bcea5158f19cdc286a9380a538cbeece583b06271"},"suggested_fix":"Remove a pending remote at the same origin in addRemote, and throw ClaxApiError(status: 502, code: 'remote_refused') for a machine name over 64 characters or with a control character.","summary":"FakeRemoteApi.addRemote keeps an earlier pending remote at the same origin and takes any machine name, where the core replaces the pending one and the remote refuses a long name","tags":["area:remote","test","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/fake_remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:39:33.744665Z","id":"41def709ed29753b8cdf50d12a95e13a7dde19dc5052258fc8e415ff4847a455","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8b23e6c85","summary":"FakeRemoteApi.addRemote now replaces a pending remote at the same origin and refuses a trimmed machine name over 64 characters or with a control character as 502 remote_refused. just test-affected 89edc6a8d at ddf502152: 284 tests pass; test/remote/fake_remote_api_test.dart 'a new sign-in replaces the pending one…' and 'a machine name over 64 characters…' failed with either rule removed.","supersedes":"2421136325f581e612f2cdbd570ac91cf2f839a89004ace68ce69cc70ac704dc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/link_remote.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:42:52.602281Z","id":"03468b950f1b496d5f4bab296f82f288f6989457ac8a2e36eea9ddac05cabfb3","body":{"detail":"resolve links again at AppLink.baseRemoteVersion, so a copy that moved meanwhile (a web edit or an editor's publish) should make the next publish answer Moved through the core's remote_n check (FakeRemoteApi.publish throws RemoteMoved when copy.current.n != link.remoteN). test/remote/publisher_test.dart covers relinking only on an unmoved copy (publish_after_disconnect_and_reconnect_lands_on_the_same_copy); a change that relinked at the head instead would pass every test and overwrite the newer public version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"80ab7b974decdd1a525556a857e98114397c14ec4d1244e9db4b408743739468"},"suggested_fix":"Add a publisher test: publish v1, removeRemote, push a version to the copy as another editor, connect again, publish v2 → Moved.","summary":"No test pins relinking when the public copy moved while this device was disconnected","tags":["area:remote","test","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/checker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:58:15.905779Z","id":"6fee144c9236fa41fa4b26d65a3874978da9f25144963342bcb64d25c88d8e24","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.7 lists three times to check: on foreground (at most once per 15 minutes per remote, LinkedChecker.onForeground), when a linked app opens (onOpen), and in the platform's background refresh where available. Only the first two exist. An app left in the background for days shows no ↓ badge or update offer, and an automatic update (AppLink.autoUpdate) does not run, until Clax comes to the front. A background task would have to open the embedded core (lib/core/) outside the UI's lifecycle, keep the UI-isolate-only-draws rule, and stay within the platforms' budgets; it is out of scope for docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-21-app-push-pull.md.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"5f17dfc64a54715f758576e5e98160324a17246ca6f4d873386642da3f807b38"},"summary":"Linked apps are checked only while Clax runs in front: no background refresh (Android WorkManager, iOS BGAppRefresh) reads their heads","tags":["spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.7","area:remote","status:deferred","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/checker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:14:04.001580Z","id":"5eb0341094118041f1e7f7c829d18943362db285694d150a07c4e0496bce8675","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.7 says the app checks on foreground at most once per 15 minutes per remote, using the remote's existing linked-artifact polling. RemoteApi has no call that reads every linked copy at once, so LinkedChecker.onForeground reads one head per linked app at a remote whose last round was 15 minutes or more ago (test/remote/checker_test.dart checker_rate_limits_per_remote_on_injected_clock). With many linked apps at one remote a round is many requests.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"c92b0feb66761828e340d776c3e1ff2d7609b5111a6e1b67745338f62103dab5"},"suggested_fix":"A batch head route (or the core's linked polling) once one exists, keeping the per-remote round.","summary":"'At most one fetch per remote per 15 minutes' is read as one round per remote: a round reads each linked app's head there","tags":["spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.7","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:15:17.567749Z","id":"e17feba4923c77c8b95cda28ad1c64daac22f15c06dbbb10fc54d3451fa8de93","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:46d7caef5","summary":"test/remote/publisher_test.dart 'a publish goes past the copy’s latest bundle version (the head floor)' passes at 46d7caef5 and fails with atLeast: null (Expected Published, Actual Refused; target/t10-pub-mut.log).","supersedes":"e28fa960c66102079834f2bd7a0f647111c3e31fee02327cbeddb0dd655b7676","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:06.461141Z","id":"01afe828b7da7a9ec81e401f03f3674b3287e876741fdb1606f6579daefc5b06","body":{"detail":"syncState sets localMoved when the copy moved and the head carries no bundle of its own (webMade, sync_state.dart:79-82), so an author with no local versions past the base is Diverged (⑂, Bring into mine / Combine, Take theirs, Publish as a new app). Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.4 defines Diverged as 'both moved: local versions beyond the shared base, and a newer public head' and Update waiting as 'public head newer than what this device last took; the local app is unmodified'; §5.10's Take theirs covers web-made heads but is listed only under Diverged. The reading avoids an Update that has no bundle to take, but it departs from the table. Separately, webMade is head.bundle?.version != head.version, so on a second author device a version another author device pushed whose bundle upload is still pending (Publisher's pendingBundle, retried until it lands) reads as Diverged until the bundle lands, then as Update waiting.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"0161b72b7b848830b9935e6adde2f06a63423bdf6f375d9cb18c34e02a1210b5"},"suggested_fix":"Owner: confirm that an unmoved author over a web-made head is Diverged (and amend §5.4), or give Update waiting a Take theirs action for that case.","summary":"An unmoved author over a web-made head reads as Diverged, where the §5.4 table's conditions give Update waiting; and a head whose bundle is still uploading reads as web-made","tags":["area:remote","spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.4","spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.10","status:needs-decision","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:06.461244Z","id":"c491cae3df58292913df19507923ad159580a77bd422244f94020d70f8e95d71","body":{"detail":"publishOrWait answers null when Publisher.waiting holds the app and lets the publish go on; only Publisher.published reports a publish that lands. A publish that later ends Refused or Moved (the copy changed meanwhile) is logged by nobody but Publisher's own log, so ReplyHold keeps the reply held for that version (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/reply_hold.dart publishAndReply) and the thread page keeps saying the reply waits, after it told the person 'Clax publishes vN when it can' (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _publishVersion).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"d35d54f8ff7b2df1c1705b685f9c9f36fbefc358c452b80987b951a697a1f82c"},"suggested_fix":"Give Publisher a stream of finished outcomes (or a per-app last outcome) and show a Refused/Moved one on the thread page and in the inbox, as record 13e53510 asks for automatic publishes.","summary":"Once publishOrWait answers null, the publish's later outcome (Refused, Moved) reaches nobody: the held reply stays held with no word on the thread page","tags":["area:remote","spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.11","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:53:12.811882Z","id":"ca1614228d9e05da78854e9850492aa13d2c435d330f1b88d23922f56a8f01cb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0edcbcdc2","summary":"Publisher.ended reports every publish's outcome as it ends; apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart keeps the last Refused or Moved publish per app (_notPublished, cleared when one lands) and LinkedAppHooks.heldNote gives the held card on the thread page its sentence (ThreadDetail.heldNote). Tests at 0edcbcdc2: test/remote/publisher_test.dart 'every publish tells how it ended…', test/ui/app_screen_remote_test.dart 'a held reply whose background publish was refused says why', test/app_remote_test.dart 'a held reply whose publish ends moved after the wait says why…' pass, and fail with _ended.add removed (the first and third: 'never reached: the held reply’s note') or with ThreadDetail ignoring the note (the second). just test-affected 0efee33d8 at 0edcbcdc2: 191 tests pass (target/t10c.log). The inbox's thread page has no held card yet (record 22b07d37).","supersedes":"c491cae3df58292913df19507923ad159580a77bd422244f94020d70f8e95d71","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:23:46.509555Z","id":"9813e279e7f24e9a3e52bc3a9ca22e9e6dc1290e8599d86f413985b325d3c9b0","body":{"detail":"For an app with no link, an ask naming another remote than a publish of the same version on its way starts its own publish (_start). Publisher.publish queues it behind the first (_publishing), and by the time it runs the first has landed and linked the app, so _publish resolves that link and pushes with link.remoteId (publisher.dart, 'rid: link?.remoteId ?? rid'): the version goes to the first remote's copy a second time. A scratch test showed it on 2aa2a7758: two connected remotes, two 503s, publish(aid, version: 1, rid: A) then publish(aid, version: 1, rid: B), clock advanced; result [(https://clax.example, 2)], one copy with two versions and nothing on the other remote. The branch also registers its publish in _onTheWay only after store.entry answers, so a third ask in that gap starts another. RemoteFlows.publish names the first connected remote for an app with no link (remote_flows.dart _connected), so no UI path reaches the branch today; it has no test of its own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":238},"end":{"line":246},"content_hash":"0e35afb3b4150120dc190956c0f3e5e5360541e2f71c6407b62eb4fa6d4b504c"},"suggested_fix":"For an app with no link, join the publish on its way whatever remote it names (one publish creates the link), or refuse the second ask in a sentence; register synchronously.","summary":"An app not linked yet, asked to publish one version to two remotes, pushes it twice to the first remote and never to the second","tags":["area:remote","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T13:38:29.121118Z","id":"7b9774065cfcdb8f037f4af864ae5314d70dcd2b32555f97287e1937fdac3136","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"01afe828b7da7a9ec81e401f03f3674b3287e876741fdb1606f6579daefc5b06","summary":"Implemented the spec §5.4 table as written: an unmoved author over a web-made head reads Update waiting (commit 418b0e0ec, lib/remote/sync_state.dart and lib/remote/checker.dart, with tests in test/remote/sync_state_test.dart). Its update is Take theirs: lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart update() shows WebVersionSheet ('Update <title> to vN?') and runs Merger.resolveDiverged(takeTheirs), which reads the head's files and publishes them locally (test/remote/merge_test.dart take_theirs_from_web_head_reads_files_and_publishes_locally). The decision stays open for the owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T13:38:29.121584Z","id":"5d187b8958845833d5213817fe11d43a1d9f367ff49d7c9a798d5a824dc9655e","body":{"detail":"RemoteApi.link (POST /api/remotes/{rid}/links) and RemoteApi.comment (POST /api/remotes/{rid}/artifacts/{raid}/comments) have no route in crates/clax-server/src on this branch (grep finds only /api/hosted/links and /api/artifacts/{aid}/threads/{tid}/comments). Merger._rebase (lib/remote/merge.dart:451) and RemoteFlows.tellOwner (lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:503) are tested only against FakeRemoteApi; against the real core they fail until those routes land. Merger._rebase also assumes POST links on an already-linked app moves its base rather than refusing a second link.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":296},"content_hash":"3bf603655c1be09fa87c9a63e9e003bbf4dfd4b8dd27748d3509deccc9c7ada3"},"summary":"Combine's re-base and Tell @owner call core routes this branch's core does not serve","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T13:38:29.121716Z","id":"cc957c45c4f862d4fe94d9db54830c02a62d2916069d723ca17e16af541a79c8","body":{"detail":"_keptFiles answers {} when the app has no kept bundle (or it cannot be read), so the merge prompt sees every file of both sides as added since the base. Claude can still combine them, but the three-way view is lost; an app that took its release before bundles were kept hits this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":505},"end":{"line":515},"content_hash":"0ead860530a79251f5343fbdbbddef2520206368c08d8397b565825a66675eb9"},"summary":"Bring vN into mine with no kept bundle merges over an empty base","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T13:38:29.121859Z","id":"e8ef5e585b509d170a0bd0c5151db82c420346164159b8f8b83798f0a88cd040","body":{"detail":"Publish mine as a new app (publishAsNewApp here, from the diverged sheet and the Kept mine card) exists, but the §5.12 fork publish of an installed app under a new title, and an app-screen pill or toast for a diverged app (the card's 'Resolve…' in lib/ui/remote/remote_card.dart and the launcher's ⑂ badge are the only entries), are left for a later task. The hosted copy made by Publish as a new app is not given forked_from by the app's push.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":480},"end":{"line":486},"content_hash":"d63461b5e622084d7ca85051d617b7ecd11c2fc1004f877ae31f38fc872382da"},"summary":"Spec §5.12's Publish fork ('<title> (yours)') and the app screen's Diverged pill are not built","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:46.380520Z","id":"23998a10e6e4317e96ab8acf7d47f5c20ec671e02058b07b15eaea510022e43e","body":{"detail":"_takeTheirs' bundle path refuses a bundle whose content_sha256 differs from the head's. Its web-made path takes whatever versionFiles answers and records it as a release without comparing contentHash(files) to head.contentSha256. It also publishes the live version's capabilities rather than the head's. A capability change made on the web is dropped silently. And when the files or capabilities differ, syncState (lib/remote/sync_state.dart, the author's head.contentSha256 != liveContentSha256 test) reads the app as Ahead right after Take theirs said it took the head.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"3464b5fa1bbce802d55754cf8d69ee01a4f19b74e1fe66a6d94cf05bbe9d58e1"},"suggested_fix":"Compare contentHash of the files read to head.contentSha256 and refuse on a mismatch, as the bundle path does. Show added capabilities from the head on WebVersionSheet and take them on Update.","summary":"Take theirs from a web-made head neither checks the files read against head.contentSha256 nor takes the head's capabilities","tags":["review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:46.380605Z","id":"8a454a505d58a88dfb40ba1c5c2e284cbef8f9ff78fca1fee63bc13e93bd0b40","body":{"detail":"The recipient branch answers live for anything that is not an update. Spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.4 defines Live as the live version's content hash and capabilities equal to the head's, which a modified copy's are not. Before syncBadge (same file) and the tile badges, this showed only on Overview's pill. Now every changed installed app shows the cloud on the launcher and the home app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"517534e7947e6acf9d5fe5d21c68af065af555c4ea280d92f8acaf20dae6143e"},"suggested_fix":"Answer a state with no badge for a modified recipient with no update (the table has no row for it: ask the owner whether it is Kept mine or a new 'Changed here'), or pass modified into the recipient branch and return no badge.","summary":"A recipient's modified copy with no newer bundle reads Live, so its tile now shows the cloud badge","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:46.381189Z","id":"edb7af648f3862071c9124ba1771807504e11da37d3949ca64a9771680c74f1f","body":{"detail":"PromptBuilder.mergePrompt (lib/agent/prompt.dart) heads the diff 'What <from> changed from the starting point', and with base {} every file of theirs is all added. Its instruction 'Bring those changes into the draft' then asks to replace each of the person's files, while 'keep every change the person made' cannot be followed without a base. Two cheaper fixes: for a linked app, read the base as remote.versionFiles(rid, raid, link.baseRemoteVersion), as _combine does. Otherwise, when base is empty, say no common starting point is known and give theirs whole rather than as an all-added diff.","kind":"comment","references":"cc957c45c4f862d4fe94d9db54830c02a62d2916069d723ca17e16af541a79c8","span":{"start":{"line":505},"end":{"line":515},"content_hash":"0ead860530a79251f5343fbdbbddef2520206368c08d8397b565825a66675eb9"},"summary":"Over an empty base the merge prompt misstates what the other side changed: it tells Claude to bring every file in whole","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:54:37.928020Z","id":"b7b79882c4c16095d2643ee89677a2435b12c1d6584139298d0f3bc8daf5ff9e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8a454a505d58a88dfb40ba1c5c2e284cbef8f9ff78fca1fee63bc13e93bd0b40","summary":"The owner's answer: \"If someone shares their app, it's functionally a fork until reset, merged, etc.\" Implemented in ffc353e15: syncState gives a recipient's modified copy with no newer bundle SyncState.forked (tile badge 'fork', ⑂, in lib/ui/launcher.dart SyncTileBadge and apps/clax_app/home/sync.js; card pill '⑂ Changed here'). Reset (the live version is a release taken) reads Live again; Bring vN into mine records the hash it published as AppLink.mergedSha256 (lib/bundle/updater.dart _applyPending), and while that is live the copy reads Live; a later change makes it a fork again. A fork with a newer bundle waiting reads Update waiting (↓), as before, so its update stays offered. Tests: test/remote/sync_state_test.dart rows 'is a fork', 'reset to the release it took is live again', 'merged in … is live again', 'changed again after a merge is a fork'; test/bundle/updater_test.dart 'a release brought into the person’s version records what it published as merged'. Left open for the owner to close.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:54:37.928283Z","id":"7770610aef0474b14aa01f280ff2c5124c0c6eeacb20f5566c1ebd54b74b2dbd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dd89f2ff8","summary":"Built: Publisher.publishFork with the Publish fork sheet (name prefilled '<title> (yours)'), and the push's forked_from for Publish fork and Publish as a new app (dd89f2ff8); the app screen's Diverged pill (dc2237d19). test/remote/publisher_test.dart 'Publish fork' group, test/remote/merge_test.dart new_app_relinks_with_forked_from (fresh.forkedFrom), test/ui/app_screen_remote_test.dart 'a diverged app shows Diverged on the pill' pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:remote_publisher_test //apps/clax_app:remote_merge_test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_remote_test: PASSED).","supersedes":"e8ef5e585b509d170a0bd0c5151db82c420346164159b8f8b83798f0a88cd040","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:54:38.070423Z","id":"5c6985457917830a69a1cbd3021c5db0d66c22cb5077462ef06392b027f57e75","body":{"detail":"HttpRemoteApi.publish sends {mode:'app', version, remote?, title?, forked_from?} (title names a fork's new copy, forked_from the public artifact it was made from); the core's PushBody (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs) is deny_unknown_fields and on this branch takes neither mode 'app' nor these fields, so every fork push is refused until the core's app-mode push accepts them. RemoteHead.capabilities comes from the hosted head route (added in 86357646b), which the core's /api/remotes/{rid}/artifacts/{raid}/head proxy must pass through; without it Combine tells the agent the other side's declaration is not known and keeps the person's. Tested only against FakeRemoteApi.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":227},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"f097f4201750ef9081ed3976b71cf29af996df3ea32767e16bd738b6e1b1ab1d"},"summary":"The app push now sends title and forked_from, and reads capabilities from the head: the local core must accept and pass them","tags":["risk","dependency","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/sync_state.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:54:38.070526Z","id":"2266a39b7047b8834d55af670d2d283cb0cf43fee4dad8c73e861c0a1d547476","body":{"detail":"Keeps the update offered: the app screen's ↓ pill, the update toast and the checker's update handling all key on SyncState.updateWaiting (lib/ui/app_screen.dart _updateTo, lib/remote/checker.dart). Showing ⑂ there would need those to offer the modified-copy update from Forked too.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"1862680e9d6897165c4d6c8d2ca333fbfebbc58bb1faef62deb019c5e5bb5b1a"},"summary":"A recipient's fork with a newer bundle waiting reads Update waiting (↓), not Forked (⑂)","tags":["revisit:if-the-owner-wants-the-fork-badge-over-an-update","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:24:44.817862Z","id":"3e8b46b7271766c817461e4c993132fcbe7c041b6b41ee92c23a7d1b20abcc35","body":{"detail":"_vet uses addedCapabilities (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:40), which compares top-level keys and net hosts only. A merged version that keeps the key db but adds db.share.read: [<another app>] or db.read entries passes the clamp and is not listed on MergedOfferSheet. docs/contract.md 'Reading another app's documents' lets app A read B when B's db.share.read lists A, with no owner grant. An injected merge could therefore open the person's documents to another app on the device. This needs that app's local ID, which an outside author is unlikely to know. The update sheets share the same blind spot.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":372},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"7218179ddb2145e597a4f290daee884c7d429d218b716d7663eaa8102dc97ddc"},"suggested_fix":"Extend CapabilityDelta to db.read and db.share.read entries (and any other list-valued capability), and use it in _vet, the offer, UpdateSheet and the checker's auto-update stop.","summary":"The merge clamp and the offer's 'also asks to' list see only top-level capabilities and net hosts, not db.read or db.share.read entries","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102103Z","id":"5bbeae030b46d61a413936702f73f53f16057feaa73c85eb3618caa6170199b6","body":{"detail":"Publisher._publish resolves the link once (line 345) and then waits in _retrying on a transient push failure, up to maxRetry (5 minutes) between tries. RemoteFlows.unpublish (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:646-705) deletes the copy, the core's unpublish route ends its link (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs unpublish), and the lineage link is set to null, but nothing stops the waiting publish. Its next try pushes with no core link, which makes a new public copy, and the store.update at line 420 finds e.link null and writes a fresh AppLink to it. The person sees the app on the remote again, Restricted, with the data choice of the original publish, after they unpublished it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":413},"end":{"line":442},"content_hash":"2e2e09778e5ee858a267a0875180c281e3dd1d8388750956a9921b03a0a2b613"},"suggested_fix":"Give Publisher a cancel for an app (called by Unpublish and Disconnect) that ends a publish waiting in _retrying as Refused; or, after the push, refuse to write a link when the lineage's link was removed since the publish began (compare remoteArtifactId with the one resolved at the start).","summary":"Unpublish while a publish of the same app waits to retry publishes the app again as a new public copy","tags":["review","lifecycle","untested","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102232Z","id":"8715f3d101e465d6a34771248b8746cda35863a609478e5c0b9bd8b92c7c9d44","body":{"detail":"bringIntoMine and _combine (lines 460-520) read the live files (_liveFiles) before the merge run, which takes minutes. Nothing marks the app busy for the worker meanwhile (Updater's busy check covers only the change in progress when Updater.update or takeFiles starts), so a comment's change can land a new version during the run. Updater.update and takeFiles then read the live version again and publish the merged files pinned to it (ifVersion: base, apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:343 and :880), so the version they replace is the change's, and its edits are gone from the live app (they stay in Versions) with nothing told.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"c6fd0cc0a1e2a8c33c97adb3b14f27e409dd8bd63a8ece0d7670a4241c8fb18c"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the live version the merge read to Updater.update/takeFiles as the version to pin to, so a change landing meanwhile fails the publish as moved; or hold the worker's changes on the app while a merge runs.","summary":"A change that lands while Claude merges is overwritten by the merged version, built from the version before it","tags":["review","concurrency","untested","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/link_remote.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102514Z","id":"6ed6e5921a1218fd7927ea8964b082d881d2bcba19068619c0c54ee12eda062b","body":{"detail":"AppRoot._connect and RemoteFlows._connected call relinkAll after any sign-in at an origin. relinkAll re-links each app linked there through the new remote and keeps the stored AppLink.role, so after Disconnect and a sign-in as a different account the apps the first account owned still read as authors here: Ahead pills, Publish vN, automatic publishing and the core's link with access 'editor' (resolve, lines 64-74), which the remote then refuses. Nothing re-reads the role from the new account's library (RemoteApi.apps).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"a5d9ce6e69014dd7a8a078c608928588f8e785b5a2adda6d7b3cd34f79eeef98"},"suggested_fix":"On relink, read the new account's library and set each link's role from RemoteApp.mayPublish, or keep the account's public ID on AppLink and leave links of another account unlinked until the person chooses.","summary":"A sign-in as another account at the same origin relinks every app to it, keeping roles the earlier account had","tags":["review","untested","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102611Z","id":"076b040dbd95792ed90ee5d587c6b6cdc4d9bac4fbfd19d3961cb3ea3ae56ec4","body":{"detail":"Replies held for local version N (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/reply_hold.dart) go out when a publish makes any version at or above N public (AppRoot._startBundles' Publisher.published listener, apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart). Take theirs replaces the local versions after the base with the head and keeps the held replies, so the next publish of a later version tells those threads 'Made this change in version N' for a change that is no longer in the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"71a0b6e570d385e46cc7f9c1582927c4c1f7fa5c2d773606714e03e397f27c4d"},"suggested_fix":"On Take theirs drop (or hold for the person) the replies held for versions above the link's old base.","summary":"Take theirs leaves held replies for the discarded local versions, which the next publish posts as fixed","tags":["review","untested","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102715Z","id":"0e70238be161bf995860a5c77658b68a1cb8ebbc9e6a16dafb3e3448a191827e","body":{"detail":"Refused(e.message) here (also lines 557, 586, 599, 605), PullRefused(e.message) (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/puller.dart:133, 163), DivergeFailed(e.message) (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart:296) and MergeFailed(e.message) (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:1557-1559) show a ClaxApiError's message, the core's or the remote's text, as the sheet's sentence, where elsewhere userMessage maps such errors. The sentences around them also differ in form for one failure: 'Couldn’t reach <host>.' (merge.dart, puller.dart), '<host> can’t be reached right now.' (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _whyNotPublic), 'The publish could not finish.' beside 'Couldn’t read this app to publish it.' (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":340},"end":{"line":410},"content_hash":"3659ade7c3521c0e6fffc1d175395d5a122b47b9b35d7c4764924a690e8ba8d0"},"suggested_fix":"Map ClaxApiError to the person's sentence at the edge (userMessage, with codes such as not_permitted, comments_off and bundle_* given their own sentences) and put the raw message under Details; settle on one form per failure.","summary":"Remote and core error messages reach the publish, pull and diverged sheets as they are, and the failure sentences vary in form","tags":["review","copy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/puller.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102906Z","id":"ef20c302136ba006b80f82aab156ce64e9b2cc0e9a7bd6c8c27644c3ff3aa4c3","body":{"detail":"role is author only when `known?.mayPublish` (line 215), and known is null when the device was not signed in at the copy's origin (rid null) or when _libraryEntry's GET /api/remotes/<rid>/apps failed (it logs and answers null, line 258-260). Nothing moves the role later: LinkRemotes.resolve (lib/remote/link_remote.dart:56-86) and relinkAll keep it, Publisher._publish refuses a recipient ('Only its owner and the people who can edit it can publish this app.'), and syncState never shows Ahead for it. Failing input: the owner taps Get in Clax on clax.dev on a phone not yet connected, or while the apps read times out, then connects; the app on that phone can never publish.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":216},"content_hash":"f9716eaafe94b8eb0687df89218dab531950badbb75a05c0675b6619510f7ad7"},"suggested_fix":"Re-derive the role from GET /api/remotes/<rid>/apps when a link is resolved onto a newly signed-in remote (relinkAll) and when a recipient's publish is refused for role, and update AppLink.role from the library's access.","summary":"A pulled app's role is decided once, at the pull: a device not signed in then, or whose library read failed, keeps the owner's or editor's app as a recipient for good","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/puller.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102943Z","id":"5b71212b137187130eb448fcede65d1ef61e64756484155a5557599866abfaf0","body":{"detail":"When remote.link fails here the error is only logged, but the AppLink stored by installer.install already names remoteId rid. LinkRemotes.resolve relinks the core only when the connected remote's ID differs from the stored one (lib/remote/link_remote.dart:62), so it never retries. For an author link the next Publisher._publish pushes in app mode with no core link; crates/clax-server/src/public.rs push_app then creates a new public artifact, and Publisher (lib/remote/publisher.dart:434-441) writes was.copyWith(url: pushed.url, baseRemoteVersion: pushed.remoteVersion) while remoteArtifactId (which copyWith cannot change) still names the original copy. Head reads, sharing and the checker then follow the old copy while pushes and bundles go to the new one. Failing input: the network drops between the bundle fetch and POST /api/remotes/<rid>/links during Get my apps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":223},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"8eca3a854bc8f5d25d47fb2960d9e321b04e3187df71cd46fb147f296969a94d"},"suggested_fix":"Store the link with remoteId null when the core link fails (resolve then makes it on next use), or have Publisher refuse an author publish whose PushResult.remoteArtifactId differs from the stored link's.","summary":"A core link refused or lost at pull time is never made again, so the author's next publish makes a second public copy and the app's link mixes the two","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.103001Z","id":"36f1f8d98ed6fda1954082d4515187523f44f9d768a957e437c3a84da2f6e4d1","body":{"detail":"HttpRemoteApi.poll copies id, origin, name, status and personName from the core's {remote, status} answer but not person_public_id, which Remote.fromJson reads and lib/agent/author_trust.dart:21 compares to a publisher's public ID. Today author_trust reads remotes() instead, so nothing compares the polled remote; any caller that keeps the connect sheet's Remote and compares accounts reads every publisher as another account.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"06015b052204c9c7be1cf7a39ffc9b593d8b23a421d4e2fd9aba36d35220b12a"},"suggested_fix":"Pass personPublicId: r.personPublicId in the rebuilt Remote.","summary":"poll rebuilds the Remote without personPublicId, so the remote a connect answers lacks the account's public ID","tags":["review","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.103594Z","id":"8f93f5103f5482a8e21567a9e8fc612b0c9d0c2f98d630b203baf0078cf9bbc4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5d187b8958845833d5213817fe11d43a1d9f367ff49d7c9a798d5a824dc9655e","summary":"Both routes are served now: crates/clax-server/src/router.rs mounts POST /api/remotes/{id}/links (remote_apps::link, which moves an existing link's base: crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs link_remote ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE) and POST /api/remotes/{id}/artifacts/{raid}/comments (remote_apps::comment). Covered by crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes_app.rs link_without_push_then_app_push_bases_on_it, relink_moves_an_existing_links_base and comment_posts_on_the_public_copy. Proposed for close by the owner as obsolete.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.103903Z","id":"24c8922659a47f93ffbc46164b0ba92cec01bfd4350770994468bfa1192e6a14","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"26fd1d7e6cc6b66aede9e2accd39cd17c1086be0ca86d6279e920fc7599b9b28","summary":"Checked against the routes as built: remote_apps::version_files passes the remote's GET /api/artifacts/<raid>/versions/<n>, {version: {files: {path: meta}}}, and remote_apps::apps passes GET /api/hosted/apps, a bare JSON array (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs list_apps). The `{apps: [...]}` branch in HttpRemoteApi.apps is never answered and can go. Proposed for close by the owner once it does.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.104192Z","id":"15265c1c0823bf114843f471d34bd7d0b695bb6774a5887edd8f64d989217912","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5c6985457917830a69a1cbd3021c5db0d66c22cb5077462ef06392b027f57e75","summary":"The core accepts these now: PushBody (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs) takes mode app with version, title and forked_from, and the head proxy (remote_apps::head) passes the remote's head body, capabilities included. Covered by crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes_app.rs app_push_of_a_new_copy_records_forked_from and app_push_names_the_copy_it_makes. Proposed for close by the owner as fixed.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:58.314076Z","id":"559bd822500db870d6407e06ba05d3c5e1a70ccaa7187170a957ca064b4b03f4","body":{"detail":"_combine reads theirs = versionFiles(head.version) and base = versionFiles(link.baseRemoteVersion) and hands the merge source: VersionSource.account(link.remoteOrigin, head.publishedBy); the app's _merge (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _merge) asks AuthorTrust.ensureSource about that one account. When the copy moved by several versions (an editor the person never trusted published v5, then the owner's other device or a trusted editor published v6), PromptBuilder.mergePrompt's base-to-theirs diff carries v5's code to Claude while only v6's publisher was asked about. The same holds for _takeTheirs's web-made path, which records only head.publishedBy as liveFrom.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":460},"end":{"line":500},"content_hash":"fd8e3a680557fa795d442cb6efab8b8ddd5e10571805cf5528c126b3e8dc7a04"},"suggested_fix":"Ask about each distinct publisher of the public versions after the base (the remote's version list names them), or, when they cannot be read, about every one the head reports; record each kept answer as ensureSource does.","summary":"Combine asks the person to trust only the head's publisher, but the diff Claude reads covers every public version since the base, which other editors may have published","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:58.314129Z","id":"7531db2aecbd947755748922c8d82118f530a22d8350b1a0347fb3d1fde4de18","body":{"detail":"_leaving calls remote.unlink (line 607) at once and only then _queue's the new-copy publish, although its doc says it 'runs after any publish of [aid] on its way'. If a publish of the same app is in _retrying (waiting for a connection, e.g. the diverged app's last publish), its push lands after the unlink: the core, no longer linked, makes a new public copy instead of answering remote_moved; _publish then writes was.copyWith(url: pushed.url, ...) (line 434), which keeps the old remoteArtifactId, so the link names copy 1's ID with copy 2's address; and the queued new-copy push then goes to copy 2 (now linked in the core) as its next version rather than making a fresh copy. Unlink is a local core call, so this happens offline too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":579},"end":{"line":620},"content_hash":"4e8e5f8528c688826a8b781b675e26b065a31ba40dbe8b5e061de44e9303769d"},"suggested_fix":"Run the unlink inside the app's _queue (before the asNew _publish, after any publish on its way), and have the non-asNew branch of _publish take remoteArtifactId from pushed (or refuse when pushed.remoteArtifactId differs from the link's).","summary":"Publish as new app ends the core's link outside the app's publish queue, so a publish waiting to retry then makes a new copy and the link mixes the old copy's ID with the new copy's URL","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:58.314173Z","id":"e95b18a59cbffa35a7f1e2c62bf59e87f59b3049f9c06d9897dec72d9152e5c1","body":{"detail":"_exchange throws _tooLarge() (line 480: code bundle_too_large, message 'the bundle is over 32 MiB') whenever the body passes cap, but anonymousHead and recordInstall call _fetch with cap: _jsonCap (1 MiB). Puller._pull maps status 413 to 'This app is too large to get.' (lib/remote/puller.dart:162) for a head read, and other callers show the 32 MiB message, both wrong for an oversized or hostile JSON answer from an arbitrary host (clax:get?url= accepts any https host).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":594},"end":{"line":608},"content_hash":"e3c35f95b09428884617b97cd0d520d45f6a8b00136149749134fc5a255ffbd6"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the error to raise with the cap (bundle_too_large for bundles, bad_response 'the answer from <origin> is too large' for JSON), and keep 'too large to get' for the bundle fetch only.","summary":"Any remote answer over its cap is reported as 413 'the bundle is over 32 MiB', including a head or install answer over the 1 MiB JSON cap","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:22:54.246877Z","id":"25e8b8e38bea73539ded16a8b6583ae235f83ee36553256cbbe81655b2b53cc8","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart:478-495 reads theirs at head.version and base at link.baseRemoteVersion and passes source: VersionSource.account(link.remoteOrigin, head.publishedBy). apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:1351-1372 _merge calls _authorTrust.ensureSource for that one source only. docs/contract.md:1271-1273 states each version names its publisher, 'the owner, or an editor', so versions between base and head can have other publishers. _takeTheirs records only head.publishedBy (merge.dart:440-443). Concern kind is right.","kind":"comment","references":"559bd822500db870d6407e06ba05d3c5e1a70ccaa7187170a957ca064b4b03f4","summary":"confirmed: _combine diffs base..head but asks trust only of head.publishedBy","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:22:54.247137Z","id":"0a32622684836931f3b4d0d5634a5df064b330a08e3cd5b8c9868026ec003d6e","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart:606-611 calls remote.unlink before _queue (:612), whose chain (:301-329) only orders _publish calls; a publish already inside _retrying (:756-771) re-calls remote.publish (:388-397) on each retry, so a retry after the unlink pushes to an unlinked app (the comment at :609 says such a push 'makes a new copy'). The non-asNew store update (:420-427) uses was.copyWith(url: pushed.url, ...) with no remoteArtifactId, keeping the old copy's ID beside the new URL. Concern kind is right (needs a retrying publish when Publish as new is chosen).","kind":"comment","references":"7531db2aecbd947755748922c8d82118f530a22d8350b1a0347fb3d1fde4de18","summary":"confirmed: _leaving unlinks outside _queue, and the non-asNew update keeps the old remoteArtifactId","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:22:54.247398Z","id":"17fd35737dc65cd9cacd3ede0a8bdfadde695883519166a6fed08d23fbae5ddc","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart:601-605 throws _tooLarge() (:480-484, 413 bundle_too_large 'the bundle is over 32 MiB') whenever the body passes cap; anonymousHead (:321-328) and recordInstall (:439-447) call _fetch with cap: _jsonCap (1 << 20, :450). lib/remote/puller.dart:162 maps 413 from the head read to 'This app is too large to get.'. Suggestion kind is right.","kind":"comment","references":"e95b18a59cbffa35a7f1e2c62bf59e87f59b3049f9c06d9897dec72d9152e5c1","summary":"confirmed: _fetch throws the 32 MiB bundle_too_large error for any cap, including the 1 MiB JSON cap","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:22:27.614755Z","id":"ecaf5603e65866bd0e433d08209c0172346d2b8c4bcc748b6497dd632563b845","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:589b348c5","summary":"Fixed in 589b348c5. Test: the remote-failure wording tests in apps/clax_app/test/remote/publisher_test.dart (final refusals incl. remote_too_old and not_permitted), merge_test.dart and puller_test.dart (//apps/clax_app:remote_publisher_test, remote_merge_test, remote_puller_test). bazelisk test of the 30 touched //apps/clax_app test targets with //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze and //scripts:check_copy at b93c4d42f: 'Executed 25 out of 32 tests: 32 tests pass.' Mutation: with remoteErrorLine forced to return e.message, 1 test fails in each target.","supersedes":"0e70238be161bf995860a5c77658b68a1cb8ebbc9e6a16dafb3e3448a191827e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:22:27.695402Z","id":"9584c4702004373898f8b70af46ef1776f0702fc2672ee9bf0d53be7ac63f9e4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:edb91c91c","summary":"Fixed in edb91c91c. Test: apps/clax_app/test/remote/remote_api_test.dart 'a JSON answer over its 1 MiB cap…' (//apps/clax_app:remote_remote_api_test). bazelisk test of the 30 touched //apps/clax_app test targets with //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze and //scripts:check_copy at b93c4d42f: 'Executed 25 out of 32 tests: 32 tests pass.' Mutation: with the fix reverted it fails.","supersedes":"e95b18a59cbffa35a7f1e2c62bf59e87f59b3049f9c06d9897dec72d9152e5c1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:22:27.862290Z","id":"4a4641394269347ecfd3a7dc6cea640a07895183bfae92478bf5e5663cd3263d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:47584f55b","summary":"Fixed in 47584f55b. Test: apps/clax_app/test/remote/publisher_test.dart 'Publish as a new app waits for a publish still trying…' and apps/clax_app/test/ui/remote_flows_test.dart (Publish as a new app offline is closable) (//apps/clax_app:remote_publisher_test, ui_remote_flows_test). bazelisk test of the 30 touched //apps/clax_app test targets with //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze and //scripts:check_copy at b93c4d42f: 'Executed 25 out of 32 tests: 32 tests pass.' Mutation: running the unlink before the queue fails the publisher test; closable:false fails the new-app flow test.","supersedes":"7531db2aecbd947755748922c8d82118f530a22d8350b1a0347fb3d1fde4de18","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/publisher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:22:27.942047Z","id":"5d3833aa7f49026779507e53ba22e006f59f039a792a241e722f8b9b56ea4877","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:47584f55b","summary":"Fixed in 47584f55b. Test: apps/clax_app/test/remote/publisher_test.dart 'stop ends a publish waiting…' and apps/clax_app/test/ui/remote_flows_test.dart (Unpublish stops a waiting publish) (//apps/clax_app:remote_publisher_test, ui_remote_flows_test). bazelisk test of the 30 touched //apps/clax_app test targets with //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze and //scripts:check_copy at b93c4d42f: 'Executed 25 out of 32 tests: 32 tests pass.' Mutation: removing publisher.stop from Unpublish fails the flow test.","supersedes":"5bbeae030b46d61a413936702f73f53f16057feaa73c85eb3618caa6170199b6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:22:29.026991Z","id":"2d22e14631509ed03f1ed65184ae7846c2b0149a5a845449d2adcada20eb578e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"559bd822500db870d6407e06ba05d3c5e1a70ccaa7187170a957ca064b4b03f4","summary":"Not fixed: the choice needs the owner. The remote names a publisher only on the head (published_by) and per bundle, not per version (docs/contract.md around line 1271 lists the head's fields; the app's RemoteApi has no per-version publisher read), so asking about every publisher between the base and the head needs either a remote route that lists each version's publisher (crates/ and the hosted deploy) or a UX rule without it, e.g. when the head is more than one version past the base, ask about 'everyone who published since v<base>' as one unknown source rather than the head's publisher alone. Which of these to build is a product decision.","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/remote/merge.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T06:04:21.859166Z","id":"827a01b2f8cefd73cfaf3918283803ab9295a1624a0bb35713dbc6cbf3b5c77c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3e8b46b7271766c817461e4c993132fcbe7c041b6b41ee92c23a7d1b20abcc35","summary":"The Rust port inherits this blind spot: clax_core::capabilities::added (crates/clax-core/src/capabilities.rs:207-226) ports addedCapabilities and compares top-level names and net hosts only, so a new db.read or db.share.read entry is no addition there either. pending keeps only GATED names and db is not one, so no approval in Clax (the Permissions bar, a publish's pending_capabilities) asks about those entries.","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
